{"id":"09c1f6db0942bca8","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-cor-martins-axiom-chain.md","title":"MA Chain Conditions","display":"cor-martins-axiom-chain — MA Chain Conditions","type":"corollary","metadata":{"type":"corollary","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-cor-martins-axiom-chain","aliases":["58-cor-martins-axiom-chain"],"display":"cor-martins-axiom-chain — MA Chain Conditions","depends_on":["[[58-df-martins-axiom]]","[[58-df-ccc]]","[[58-df-poset]]","[[58-df-zfc-filter-on-poset]]","[[58-df-zfc-dense-subset-poset]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"corollary"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-cor-martins-axiom-chain"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-cor-martins-axiom-chain</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"cor-martins-axiom-chain — MA Chain Conditions"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b4f557645bc9a749\" href=\"?note=b4f557645bc9a749\" title=\"58-df-martins-axiom\">58-df-martins-axiom</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"937fc0dd4cc72948\" href=\"?note=937fc0dd4cc72948\" title=\"58-df-ccc\">58-df-ccc</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d3f859dbdd37f018\" href=\"?note=d3f859dbdd37f018\" title=\"58-df-poset\">58-df-poset</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"bafc4b7d4da7f0a7\" href=\"?note=bafc4b7d4da7f0a7\" title=\"58-df-zfc-filter-on-poset\">58-df-zfc-filter-on-poset</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"cc7ca8f5bdd5c9bc\" href=\"?note=cc7ca8f5bdd5c9bc\" title=\"58-df-zfc-dense-subset-poset\">58-df-zfc-dense-subset-poset</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> (cardinal parameter)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MA}(\\kappa)\">\\(\\mathrm{MA}(\\kappa)\\)</span> (Martin's axiom at <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"b4f557645bc9a749\" href=\"?note=b4f557645bc9a749\" title=\"58-df-martins-axiom\">58-df-martins-axiom</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(\\mathbb P,R)\">\\((\\mathbb P,R)\\)</span> (forcing poset, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"d3f859dbdd37f018\" href=\"?note=d3f859dbdd37f018\" title=\"58-df-poset\">58-df-poset</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Poset}(\\mathbb P,R)\">\\(\\mathrm{Poset}(\\mathbb P,R)\\)</span> (partial-order predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"d3f859dbdd37f018\" href=\"?note=d3f859dbdd37f018\" title=\"58-df-poset\">58-df-poset</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CCC}(\\mathbb P,R)\">\\(\\mathrm{CCC}(\\mathbb P,R)\\)</span> (countable-chain-condition predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"937fc0dd4cc72948\" href=\"?note=937fc0dd4cc72948\" title=\"58-df-ccc\">58-df-ccc</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DenseSubsetPoset}_S(D,\\mathbb P,R)\">\\(\\mathrm{DenseSubsetPoset}_S(D,\\mathbb P,R)\\)</span> (dense-subset predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"cc7ca8f5bdd5c9bc\" href=\"?note=cc7ca8f5bdd5c9bc\" title=\"58-df-zfc-dense-subset-poset\">58-df-zfc-dense-subset-poset</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcFilterOnPoset}_S(G,\\mathbb P,R)\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcFilterOnPoset}_S(G,\\mathbb P,R)\\)</span> (poset-filter predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-11\" data-note=\"bafc4b7d4da7f0a7\" href=\"?note=bafc4b7d4da7f0a7\" title=\"58-df-zfc-filter-on-poset\">58-df-zfc-filter-on-poset</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}martins-axiom-chain} \\vdash \\mathrm{MA}(\\kappa) \\to \\forall\\mathbb P\\;\\forall R\\;\\left((\\mathrm{Poset}(\\mathbb P,R)\\land\\mathrm{CCC}(\\mathbb P,R))\\to\\forall\\mathcal D\\;\\left((|\\mathcal D|&lt;\\kappa\\land\\forall D\\in\\mathcal D\\;\\mathrm{DenseSubsetPoset}_S(D,\\mathbb P,R))\\to\\exists G\\;(\\mathrm{ZfcFilterOnPoset}_S(G,\\mathbb P,R)\\land\\forall D\\in\\mathcal D\\;(G\\cap D\\neq\\emptyset))\\right)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}martins-axiom-chain} \\vdash \\mathrm{MA}(\\kappa) \\to \\forall\\mathbb P\\;\\forall R\\;\\left((\\mathrm{Poset}(\\mathbb P,R)\\land\\mathrm{CCC}(\\mathbb P,R))\\to\\forall\\mathcal D\\;\\left((|\\mathcal D|&lt;\\kappa\\land\\forall D\\in\\mathcal D\\;\\mathrm{DenseSubsetPoset}_S(D,\\mathbb P,R))\\to\\exists G\\;(\\mathrm{ZfcFilterOnPoset}_S(G,\\mathbb P,R)\\land\\forall D\\in\\mathcal D\\;(G\\cap D\\neq\\emptyset))\\right)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Under <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MA}_\\kappa\">\\(\\mathrm{MA}_\\kappa\\)</span>, every family of fewer than <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> dense subsets of a c.c.c. forcing poset is met by a generic filter.</li>\n<li>This yields many consequences like non-existence of certain mad families.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-martins-axiom","status":"resolved","id":"b4f557645bc9a749","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-martins-axiom]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-ccc","status":"resolved","id":"937fc0dd4cc72948","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excer